<![CDATA[ HY-Geo: A Hybrid Mixture-of-Experts and Hypergraph Framework for Intelligent Geological Body Detection in Borehole-Scale Electrical Imaging Logs ]]>
</title>
<link>
<![CDATA[ http://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11435196 ]]>
</link>
<description>
<![CDATA[ Electrical imaging logs, as a form of borehole-scale active remote sensing, can provide high-resolution visualization of subsurface structures such as fractures and stratifications. These geological bodies exhibit pronounced cross-scale and nonlocal spatial correlations, and their accurate detection relies on effective modeling of high-order topological relationships. However, existing automatic detection methods based on local convolutional features struggle to characterize complex stratigraphic patterns, resulting in limited accuracy and generalization capability in visually complicated borehole environments. To address these challenges, this study proposes a hybrid deep learning framework for geological body detection in electrical imaging logs, termed HY-Geo. The framework is built upon an enhanced YOLOv9 architecture and integrates a hybrid Kolmogorov–Arnold mixture-of-experts semantic processing module (HKM-SPM) together with a hypergraph convolution mechanism. This design enables the unified modeling of nonlinear semantic interactions and cross-scale, high-order topological dependencies among geological structures. A benchmark dataset containing 10 000 borehole formation microresistivity imaging (FMI) images was constructed for evaluation, covering four representative geological types, conductive fractures, resistive fractures, drilling-induced fractures, and bedding structures. Experimental results demonstrate that HY-Geo achieves an mAP@0.5:0.95 of 96.3%, a precision of 0.962, and a recall of 0.937, consistently outperforming competing methods in both detection accuracy and robustness across multiple geological categories. In terms of efficiency, HY-Geo reaches an inference speed of 43 frames per second (FPS), while its compact variant achieves up to 89 FPS, satisfying real-time interpretation requirements in field applications. These results indicate that HY-Geo provides an accurate and efficient solution for automatic geological body detection in complex borehole environments, offering reliable technical support for downhole structural interpretation and digital logging analysis. ]]>
